.TH QUILLMOTE 1 "September 2026" "Quillmote" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
quillmote \- a simple text editor for Linux
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quillmote
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Quillmote edits plain text in tabs, with find and replace, spelling,
word counts, printing, and crash recovery. Its appearance follows the desktop.
.PP
Each supplied file opens in a separate tab. If a path does not exist,
an empty document is opened with that filename; Save creates the file.
The parent directory must exist. Each launch opens an independent window.
Use \fB--\fR before filenames beginning with a dash.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the application version and exit, without opening a display.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show command-line usage and exit.
.SH SHORTCUTS
Ctrl+N or Ctrl+T creates a tab; Ctrl+O opens files; Ctrl+S saves;
Ctrl+Shift+S opens Save As. Ctrl+W closes a tab and Ctrl+Q exits.
Ctrl+Tab and Ctrl+Shift+Tab switch tabs.
.PP
Ctrl+F opens Find; Ctrl+H reveals Replace; F3 finds the next match.
Escape closes Find. Ctrl+G goes to a line. F5 inserts the date and time.
Ctrl++ and Ctrl+- zoom, and Ctrl+0 resets zoom. F1 opens the offline guide.
.SH SPELLING
Spell checking uses the optional Enchant 2 runtime and installed dictionaries.
Select a dictionary under Format, Spelling, Language.
Install extra dictionaries with the distribution's package manager, then restart.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/quillmote/settings.ini
Editor and window preferences.
.TP
.I ~/.config/quillmote/recovery/
Private snapshots of unsaved documents. Snapshots do not overwrite original files.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
Overrides the default configuration directory, ~/.config.
.SH RECOVERY
After an interrupted session, launching without files restores available snapshots
in separate tabs. When opening a file, the Recover banner offers earlier unsaved work.
Saving or explicitly discarding a document clears its snapshot.
The latest edits may not have reached a snapshot; save regularly.
